# Testing Conventions

- Follow the existing pytest structure, naming and fixture conventions.
- Use real implementations and integration-style tests where the existing project testing infrastructure supports them; use mocks/test doubles where isolated unit testing is more appropriate.
- Repository tests should exercise the real repository implementation.
- Controller tests should call controllers directly rather than unnecessarily using the Flask test client.
- Reuse existing fixtures rather than creating parallel fixture infrastructure.
- Add tests for new behaviour and regression cases introduced by a change.
- Run the relevant test suite after implementation.